<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23217" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infirmo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a. and n.
		infirmus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to deprive of
			strength</i>, <i>to weaken</i>, <i>enfeeble.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 15, 10</span></i>
			: munimenta madore, Sall. Fragm. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 138, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hominem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					2, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>To invalidate</i>, <i>disprove</i>,
				<i>refute</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res tam leves infirmare ac diluere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rosc. Am. 15, 42</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">with tollere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 2, 59, 147</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">with frangere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 131</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fidem testis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rosc. Com. 15, 45</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fidem alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 15, 26</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>To annul</i>, <i>make void</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 1, 49</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contractum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 49, 14, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">graviter ferens aliquid a se factum infirmari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					2, 2, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acta illa atque omnes res superioris anni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 18, 40</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i> only in <i>part. pres.</i>
			as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infirmantes</span></b> , um, m., <i>the weak</i>, <i>sick</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev. Vit. S. Mart. 18,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 2, 12</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
